/* book exam traps: For a four-stroke use 720°/n, not 360°/n; 360°/n is the two-stroke value. | Changing 1-3-4-2 to 1-2-4-3 does not change the firing interval; it only swaps the firing of cylinders 2 and 3. | Do not offer 1-2-3-4 for an inline four: it cannot work on a flat four-throw crankshaft. | L-head means both valves in the block; I-head means both in the head; F-head has one in each; T-head one on each side. | The half-speed camshaft rule is for four-strokes only; a two-stroke camshaft, where fitted, turns at crank speed. */
